- SA-F3: app.rs:5411-5424 — the marquee "steady ticker" pin branch can
  NEVER fire: marquee_next_step(now) returns a STRICTLY-FUTURE boundary
  (k = (now-start)/80 + 1 ⇒ start + k·80 > now), so `deadline <= now_ms`
  is always false. Clock advances only on the plain 100ms branch; wakes
  land every 80ms so the 100ms threshold fires every OTHER boundary →
  clock jumps +160ms → offset +2 cells per render → ~166ms/step. Fix:
  pin to the last PASSED boundary each iteration while scrolling.
- SA-F13: input thread (app.rs:4763-4776) loops `crossterm::event::read()`
  forever; it only exits when a key arrives after the receiver dropped.
  A second boot's thread races the zombie for crossterm's global reader
  lock; the zombie eats the first key(s) → dead chord on leg 2. Fix:
  poll(50ms)+stop-flag thread with a Drop guard (also covers cancel).
- SA-F7: VERIFIED ref pairing from ref source: `+` release → `tabs.add()`
  → `route.navigate({type:"home"})` (context/session-tabs.tsx:406-420).
  The ref does NOT create a tab; ours already navigates Home
  (app.rs:575 StripHit::Add). Disposition: parity already holds; pin with
  a test instead of changing behavior.

